//! [`Client`]: the whole game, minus the window.
//!
//! java: `client/Minecraft.java`'s `runGameLoop` (`:1083`) and `runTick` (`:1741`), plus the
//! subsystem construction in `startGame` that is not asset loading.
//!
//! # Why this is not just an `impl ShellApp`
//!
//! It *is* one — see the bottom of this file — but the trait's methods are the only part that
//! needs a window. Everything else takes an explicit `&Gpu`, a `&mut PhaseList` and a
//! `&mut Camera`, so the identical code path runs under `mc_render::Gpu::headless`. That is not
//! a testing convenience bolted on afterwards: this environment has **no display**, and a client
//! whose logic can only be exercised through a window is a client nobody here can check.
//!
//! # Render-phase handles and the arena-index rule
//!
//! `PhaseList` takes `Box<dyn RenderPhase>` and never gives it back, but several renderer parts
//! need a *per-tick driver* that mutates a phase between frames. [`Shared`] is the answer: an
//! `Rc<RefCell<T>>` that is itself a `RenderPhase`, so the list owns one handle and the game loop
//! keeps another. The arena-index rule bans `Rc<RefCell>` in the
//! world/entity graph (§11 names `mc-world`, `mc-physics`, `mc-protocol`); S11 set this exact
//! precedent for `TerrainRenderer`, and `TerrainPhase::install` hands back such a handle.

